\ A compiled word that dispatches a closure holds its owning reference in a spill. When the closure
\ raises, the word's error exit releases the spill, so an interpreter-free binary reports no leak.

\ `try` dispatches the curried quotation through a runtime call.
divide-into: ( n -- r ) [ [ 100 swap / ] curry try ] ;

0 divide-into result:err? .
5 divide-into result:ok? .
